Test code:

```ts
  /**
   * How much a change should carry — the philosophy, fixed, and not a slot.
   *
   * #216: the pull is to make a run bolder about deleting what no longer earns its
   * place, and the failure it is against is the opposite of boldness: a change that
   * works and leaves the file harder to read, which costs the next change. Two halves
   * have to survive editing. The stance itself — unreadable code is a bug of the same
   * kind, so the default is the smaller shape rather than the compatible one — and the
   * price it puts on the exceptions: a fallback or a workaround is a trade-off taken on
   * purpose, kept small, explained where it lives, and reported as a cost.
   *
   * What is pinned as well is that the section carries no placeholder. The philosophy
   * is fixed text: an adopter that could swap it would be swapping the thing that makes
   * the rest of the prompt hold together, and a slot invites the wording to drift into
   * whatever each project means by "clean".
   */
  test("the shared prompt says how much to change, as fixed text with no slot to swap it", () => {
    const raw = readFileSync("src/content/prompt-template.md", "utf8");
    const heading = "# How much to change";
    const start = raw.indexOf(heading);
    expect(start, "the section has to exist").toBeGreaterThan(-1);
    const after = raw.slice(start + heading.length);
    const end = after.indexOf("\n# ");
    const sectionRaw = end === -1 ? after : after.slice(0, end);
    const section = sectionRaw.replace(/\s+/g, " ");

    expect(section, "the defect this is against, named as the same kind as a bug").toContain(
      "Unreadable code is a defect of the same kind as a bug",
    );
    expect(section, "and why: it is what makes the next change go wrong").toContain(
      "Both are how the next change goes wrong",
    );
    expect(section, "the default is the shape that removes code").toContain(
      "prefer the shape that has less in it",
    );
    expect(section, "compatibility and fallbacks are exceptions, not the default").toContain(
      "are not the default",
    );
    expect(section, "a fallback needs a reason this project has").toContain(
      "for a reason this project actually has",
    );
    // The price of taking the exception, or it is just permission.
    expect(section, "kept small").toContain("keep it small");
    expect(section, "and explained where it lives").toContain("write why it is there at the place");
    expect(section, "and reported as a cost the next reader pays").toContain(
      "what it costs the next reader",
    );
    // No slot: the philosophy is not an adopter's setting.
    expect(sectionRaw, "the section must not offer a placeholder to swap").not.toMatch(/\{\{/);
